WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.417
Give our

00:00:00.417 --> 00:00:02.637
worker the clock job. I want one

00:00:02.637 --> 00:00:05.377
test alarm labeled Guide demo. I want

00:00:05.377 --> 00:00:07.157
it switched off, and I want that

00:00:07.157 --> 00:00:09.357
agent to check it and then delete

00:00:09.357 --> 00:00:11.197
it. If we're showing a direct command

00:00:11.197 --> 00:00:13.277
in a terminal, we'll label it as

00:00:13.277 --> 00:00:14.857
my command so you can tell which

00:00:14.857 --> 00:00:16.350
part of the agent actually did.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.070
I ask for the UI, I get

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.670
the screen on as a text, okay?

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:21.490
It shows up with labels in the

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:23.090
center of each element. So I have

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:25.590
the agent find Add alarm and then

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.690
use that point from the screen. It

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.670
just read Okay, you follow along.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.110
on the guide, you'll see in the

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:33.930
list that we've checked that it switched

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.030
off. That's the result I asked for.

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:37.730
So we can show it before the

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:41.644
agent cleans up. Then I have it

00:00:41.644 --> 00:00:43.504
delete the test alarm. Read the list

00:00:43.504 --> 00:00:45.184
again and check that the label is

00:00:45.184 --> 00:00:47.804
gone. I want the cleanup checked as

00:00:47.804 --> 00:00:48.827
well.
